    "turn_text": "There will be a Democratic president. This is an election about America. Yeah, this is an election about America. I mean, I'm not making my plans right here. And now we'll see how it goes. But that's not excluded, shall we say? It's not about Democrats or Republicans. It's about our country, about our country, about the middle class. And that's what the president said. It's so beautifully at the White House the other day. He said the middle class has a union label on it. They're trying to undermine rights of collective bargaining, organizing, undermine women who undermine environmental movements and all of that. So the fight goes on for you. The fight goes on, but I think it's a fight that the public is much more aware of now because they see what is the principle that is dividing the Republican Party. This is not the Republican Party, the grand old party that did so many great things for our country. We want the Republican Party to be a strong party, but this is a hijacked political party that is taking the party over the edge and trying to drag the country with it. And they're leaving the middle wide open for us. And that's where I think we have to go with our message as progressive as a Democrat as I am to take it to a place where we built the most consensus for the good of the American people. Middle class consumer economics to turn the economy on because what the president did His accomplishments are remarkable. They all haven't hit home for many people in our country. We have to show them why.",
